{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-53140",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/cd66b6b8c4e1a7a1deb68de79d842a21760df66d615721e933105361ea3f8af5.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠AOB$ and $∠BOC$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OB}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC & =m∠AOB+m∠BOC \\\\  & ={32}^{∘}+{46}^{∘} \\\\  & ={78}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
